'''Maavarulu Airport'''<ref name="CAA">{{cite web |title=List of Land Aerodromes in Maldives |url=https://www.caa.gov.mv/attachments/Fo0c3gdATSgFEBcEdOFPZwGEUGNaKQrHLbD8PZUS.pdf |publisher=Maldives CAA |access-date=14 February 2022}}</ref> {{Airport codes|RUL|VRQM}} is a domestic [[airport]] located on [[Maavarulu]], one of the islands of the [[Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll]] in [[Maldives]]. Scheduled Flights started on 4 July 2020.{{cn|date=February 2022}}

==Facilities==
The airport resides at an [[elevation]] of {{convert|2|m}} above [[mean sea level]]. It has one [[runway]] which is {{convert|1,200|m|0}} in length and {{convert|40|m|0}} wide.{{fact|date=June 2023}}

